-- Income Tax Act 1947 — INDEPENDENT TESTS.
-- Every expected value below was decided from ../source/ITA1947.txt before any
-- .l4 file was opened; see independent-expectations.md (scenario ids in the
-- comments). A failing assertion is a finding and is left failing.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Helpers (record builders only)`

GIVEN ei     IS A NUMBER
      ag     IS A NUMBER
      dis    IS A BOOLEAN
      fem    IS A BOOLEAN
      sp     IS A BOOLEAN
      spinc  IS A NUMBER
      spinf  IS A BOOLEAN
      kids   IS A LIST OF `Child facts`
      prem   IS A NUMBER
      cpf    IS A NUMBER
      seai   IS A NUMBER
      seob   IS A NUMBER
      deps   IS A LIST OF `Dependant facts`
      fees   IS A NUMBER
      nss    IS A `National service status`
      gpi    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      levy   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Individual relief facts`
`rf` ei ag dis fem sp spinc spinf kids prem cpf seai seob deps fees nss gpi levy MEANS
    `Individual relief facts` WITH
        `earned income` IS ei
        `age reached by 31 December of the preceding year` IS ag
        `totally blind or permanently and severely disabled` IS dis
        `a female claimant (married, divorced or widowed)` IS fem
        `had a spouse living with or maintained by the claimant` IS sp
        `spouse's income in the preceding year` IS spinc
        `spouse incapacitated by physical or mental infirmity` IS spinf
        `payments to a former spouse under a court order or deed` IS 0
        `children` IS kids
        `life insurance premiums, capped at 7% of the capital sum` IS prem
        `obligatory CPF or approved fund contributions as an employee` IS cpf
        `self-employed: assessable income from the trade or profession` IS seai
        `self-employed: obligatory CPF contributions on that income` IS seob
        `self-employed: voluntary CPF contributions` IS 0
        `dependants` IS deps
        `incapacitated siblings maintained` IS 0
        `course fees` IS fees
        `national service` IS nss
        `wife or widow of an NSman, claiming` IS FALSE
        `parent of an NSman, claiming` IS FALSE
        `SRS contributions` IS 0
        `SRS contribution cap` IS 0
        `SRS account suspended, or the contribution withdrawn in the year` IS FALSE
        `grandparent caregiver: the caregiver's trade or employment income` IS gpi
        `CPF cash top-ups for family, after grants and capped as prescribed` IS 0
        `CPF cash top-ups for self, after grants and capped as prescribed` IS 0
        `prescribed deduction limit for s 39(3)` IS 0
        `prescribed deduction limit for s 39(3A)` IS 0
        `foreign domestic worker levy paid, for one worker` IS levy

`no NS` MEANS `not an operationally ready national serviceman`

GIVEN ei IS A NUMBER
      ag IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Individual relief facts`
`basic` ei ag MEANS `rf` ei ag FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EMPTY 0 0 0 0 EMPTY 0 `no NS` NOTHING 0

GIVEN inc   IS A BOOLEAN
      cinc  IS A NUMBER
      ord   IS A NUMBER
      pd    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Child facts`
`kid` inc cinc ord pd MEANS
    `Child facts` WITH
        `unmarried throughout the preceding year` IS TRUE
        `below 16 at any time in the preceding year` IS TRUE
        `in full-time instruction` IS FALSE
        `serving under articles or indentures` IS FALSE
        `incapacitated by physical or mental infirmity` IS inc
        `income in the preceding year, excluding scholarships` IS cinc
        `engaged in employment or a trade, other than under articles` IS FALSE
        `maintained by the claimant` IS TRUE
        `claimant's share of the relief` IS 1
        `a Singapore citizen` IS TRUE
        `order among the mother's eligible children` IS ord
        `the para 5 date` IS pd

GIVEN dage  IS A NUMBER
      dinc  IS A NUMBER
      dinf  IS A BOOLEAN
      dliv  IS A BOOLEAN
      dspent IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Dependant facts`
`dep` dage dinc dinf dliv dspent MEANS
    `Dependant facts` WITH
        `a parent, grandparent or great-grandparent of the claimant or spouse` IS TRUE
        `living in Singapore` IS TRUE
        `age at any time in the preceding year` IS dage
        `income in the preceding year` IS dinc
        `incapacitated by physical or mental infirmity` IS dinf
        `living with the claimant in the same household` IS dliv
        `spent by the claimant on maintenance` IS dspent
        `claimant's share of the relief` IS 1

GIVEN rec   IS A `Kind of person`
      res   IS A BOOLEAN
      part  IS A BOOLEAN
      trd   IS A BOOLEAN
      dd    IS A DATE
      payr  IS A BOOLEAN
      pe    IS A BOOLEAN
      dys   IS A NUMBER
      dir   IS A BOOLEAN
      subj  IS A BOOLEAN
      head  IS A NUMBER
      ben   IS A BOOLEAN
      amt   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Exemption facts`
`ef` rec res part trd dd payr pe dys dir subj head ben amt MEANS
    `Exemption facts` WITH
        `recipient` IS rec
        `recipient resident in Singapore` IS res
        `received through a partnership in Singapore` IS part
        `derived from carrying on a trade, business or profession` IS trd
        `derived or paid on` IS dd
        `the payer is a company resident in Singapore` IS payr
        `the recipient has a business or PE in Singapore` IS pe
        `days employment exercised in Singapore` IS dys
        `as a director of a company` IS dir
        `as a public entertainer not substantially supported from foreign public funds` IS FALSE
        `subject to tax in the territory it comes from` IS subj
        `that territory's headline corporate rate` IS head
        `the Comptroller is satisfied the exemption is beneficial` IS ben
        `the s 13(9)(a) condition waived` IS FALSE
        `on a Singapore ship, exercised substantially outside Singapore` IS FALSE
        `amount of the income` IS amt
        `an approval or prescription covers the income` IS FALSE
        `the conditions of the paragraph are met` IS FALSE
        `the beneficiary's share would be exempt if received directly` IS FALSE

`d25` MEANS YMD 2025 6 1

GIVEN incorp IS A BOOLEAN
      resi   IS A BOOLEAN
      nsh    IS A NUMBER
      allind IS A BOOLEAN
      ten    IS A BOOLEAN
      post13 IS A BOOLEAN
      propdev IS A BOOLEAN
      invonly IS A BOOLEAN
      yinc   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Start-up facts`
`co` incorp resi nsh allind ten post13 propdev invonly yinc MEANS
    `Start-up facts` WITH
        `incorporated in Singapore` IS incorp
        `resident in Singapore for the YA` IS resi
        `limited by guarantee` IS FALSE
        `number of shareholders, directly and beneficially` IS nsh
        `all shareholders (or members) individuals throughout the basis period` IS allind
        `an individual held at least 10% throughout the basis period` IS ten
        `incorporated on or after 26 February 2013` IS post13
        `undertakes property development, itself or as a partner` IS propdev
        `its only activity is holding investments, itself or through a partnership` IS invonly
        `YA of incorporation` IS yinc

GIVEN sold   IS A DATE
      grp    IS A BOOLEAN
      oth    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Foreign asset sale`
`sale` sold grp oth MEANS
    `Foreign asset sale` WITH
        `sold on` IS sold
        `the seller is a member of a relevant group` IS grp
        `the asset is situated outside Singapore` IS TRUE
        `gains received in Singapore` IS 1000000
        `otherwise chargeable as income under s 10(1)` IS FALSE   -- encoder's plumbing edit after the field was split (see the report's triage)
        `otherwise exempt from tax` IS oth
        `an intellectual property right` IS FALSE
        `incidental to a prescribed financial institution's business, or to an incentive-income activity` IS FALSE
        `an excluded entity in the basis period` IS FALSE
        `deductible expenditure and losses` IS 0

